# GCP-0066 (LOW): Storage bucket should use customer-managed encryption key
# Deferred — Google-managed encryption is sufficient at our scale. CMEK adds
# key management overhead and lockout risk that doesn't pay off until we have
# compliance requirements that mandate it. Revisit if SOC2/etc. ever applies.
GCP-0066

# GCP-0077 (MEDIUM): Storage bucket access logging not enabled
# Deferred — would require provisioning an audit log destination bucket which
# itself triggers the same finding (recursive). Forensic value is real but
# not yet load-bearing at single-operator scale. Revisit if we ever have
# multiple humans with state access.
GCP-0077
